cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Ghost Ink in teaching or research, please cite this software."
type: software
title: "Ghost Ink: An Interactive Security Exhibit on Hidden Content and Detection Boundaries"
abstract: "An offline-capable browser-based educational security exhibit exploring hidden and deceptive content across Unicode, text rendering, clipboard interactions, transformations, and images. Interactive demonstrations pair concealment techniques with inspection, cleaning, and detection-boundary explanations. Includes optional authenticated payload encryption and documented limitations."
authors:
  - family-names: "Clark"
    given-names: "Paul A."
    affiliation: "Leon County Public Library"
